speechtext:
1. No. The Tas-chereau papers although in the possession of the security service of the RCMP were not documents generated by the security service. The so-called Featherbed file is a file of the security service. Although it has been dormant since 1975 and is dormant now, it is an operational file. Its release is not in the public interest because of some or all of the factors referred to in connection with details of foreign espionage referred to in No. 2 below.
2.	It is government policy to exempt important details of foreign espionage against Canada and related security matters from disclosure if it is in Canada's national interest to do so. Factors leading to such a policy decision include:
(a)	the probability and extent of injury to Canada's national security;
(b)	the possibility of violation of the right of privacy of an individual;
(c)	disclosure resulting in violation of any law relating to the privacy of an individual; and
(d)	injury to a confidential agreement made between the Government of Canada and any other government.
